2781 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(valuations. At the same time, real estate\nmarkets are affected by older populations\nlooking to age in place in a healthy\nenvironment with a lifestyle they enjoy.\nExpanding pools of luxury\nhomebuyers are great news for the high-\nend\302\240housing market. For sellers, this\noffers\302\240more opportunities. It means they\nneed to curate their homes for double-\nduty\302\240attractiveness, as a place where\na\302\240young millennial family and older\nhomeowners can envision themselves.\nWhere people choose to buy is just\nas\302\240revealing as why they buy. \342\200\234Location,\nlocation, location\342\200\235 is perhaps the most\niconic real estate mantra. This report\ndelves\302\240into markets that remain eternally\nattractive for luxury homebuyers alongside\nmarkets experiencing a resurgence in\nattention. The\302\240world\342\200\231s great cities\342\200\224New\nYork City, Miami, San Francisco, Los\nAngeles, London, Sydney, Singapore\nand Hong Kong\342\200\224remain centers for\nwealth\302\240creation.\nOnce generational wealth has been\nachieved, the priorities of ultra-high-\nnet-worth-individuals shift to wealth\npreservation. There\342\200\231s a push and pull,\nwith\302\240different seasons in life that draw\npeople to own homes in various places.\nFor\302\240example, while young entrepreneurs\nin\302\240tech and finance look to buy luxury\nproperties in San Francisco and New York,\na wave of ultrawealthy homebuyers\ncontinues to pour into Miami and Palm\nBeach, for the lifestyle, proximity to\nfriends\302\240and wealth preservation.)/P 55 0 R/K[3545 0 R]/Pg 12 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

