2824 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(accumulation at all income levels stems from housing\nvalue appreciation.\nWhile the general real estate market has been\nsluggish for the past three years, the upper end has\ncontinued to show signs of strength, according to\nLawrence Yun, chief economist and senior vice president\nof research, National Association of REALTORS\302\256 \(NAR\).\n\342\200\234There\342\200\231s a little more inventory that has helped keep that\nproperty market moving,\342\200\235 he says. \342\200\234The stock market\302\240has\nhelped, plus the ability of upper-end homebuyers to pay\nwith cash and not be concerned about\302\240mortgage rates.\342\200\235\nMost of the wealth in the stock market is held by\nthe\302\240top 5% of households in the U.S., Yun says, so these\npast few years of equity gains have generated the ability\nto\302\240buy second, third and fourth homes at the top tier of the\nhousing market. Luxury homeowners have also benefited\nfrom a rise in home values, so they can sell a property\nand pay cash for their next purchase, he continues.\nBut Yun believes mortgage rates still have\na psychological impact on luxury homebuyers.\nFollowing the Federal Reserve\342\200\231s April 2026 meeting,\nwhen the central bank decided to hold interest rates at\n3.5% to 3.75%, Yun expects that mortgage rates could\ncome down from lower inflationary pressures once the\nfinancial market shock over oil prices dissipates.\nLocation Matters\nLooking beyond the luxury real estate sector, in the\noverall real estate market, 2026 should be a year of\ngradual improvement in affordability according to Hepp,\nalthough there will be some variations by region and price\nrange. \342\200\234Real estate markets where homeowners and\nhomebuyers are in the upper income levels are doing\nbetter than those with lower incomes,\342\200\235 she says.\n\342\200\234Property investor\302\240activity is up and the tax benefits\nfor upper\302\240income households are likely to help the\nluxury housing market as well as investors.\342\200\235 u)/P 55 0 R/K[3573 0 R]/Pg 16 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

