<</Type/StructElem/Alt(The expansion of state and local income tax \(SALT\)\ndeductions from US$10,000 to US$40,000 in July\302\2402025\ndue to the One Big Beautiful Bill Act4 will likely increase\npurchases of high-end residences in states with high\nproperty tax rates, such as New Jersey, Connecticut,\nMassachusetts and New York, according to Yun. However,\nthe expanded deductions are phased out for taxpayers\nwith an adjusted gross income of US$500,000 or higher,\nso\302\240it may not have a significant impact on ultra-luxury\nhousing markets. \342\200\234As people filed their income tax returns\nin April, they\302\240found they could reduce their tax bill with\nSALT deductions,\342\200\235 Yun explains. \342\200\234They have extra money\nin their pockets and may be encouraged to buy a larger\nhome when they realize they can deduct more of their\nproperty\302\240taxes.\342\200\235\nIn addition, if legislation passes to increase the capital\ngains tax exemption for home sales, that could also help\nthe upper end of the housing market, Yun says. Currently\nhome sellers can exclude US$250,000 \(US$500,000 for\302\240a\nmarried couple\) of the proceeds from the sale of\ntheir\302\240home from capital gains taxes, according to IRS\nguidelines.5 \342\200\234More homeowners might consider selling\nif\302\240their tax burden is reduced, which could increase the\nnumber of high-end transactions,\342\200\235 he says.\nRising insurance costs, higher property taxes and\ninflation have much less of an impact on the ultra-luxury\nproperty market, Hepp says, but rising labor costs limit\nnew construction and slow the pace of custom\nhomebuilding. \342\200\234The unpredictability of tariffs and\nimmigration issues have made it much more difficult to\nprice custom homes,\342\200\235 she notes. \342\200\234It\342\200\231s hard to know what\nmaterials will cost because tariffs have been up and down\nand vary by item. Plus, builders struggle to estimate labor\ncosts because of\302\240concerns about immigration.\342\200\235\nLuxury Real Estate Metrics\nMore than half \(55%\) of Sotheby\342\200\231s International\nRealty affiliated real estate professionals around the\nglobe reported an increase in the number of luxury u)/P 55 0 R/K[3587 0 R]/Pg 18 0 R/S/Figure>>
