<</Type/StructElem/Alt(homebuyers in their local property markets over\nthe past 12 months, according to\302\240the 2026 Mid-Year\nSotheby\342\200\231s International Realty agent\302\240survey. They\nanticipate a similarly strong turnout throughout 2026,\nand reported average price increases\302\240of\302\2405%.\nParticularly in this top tier of the real estate market,\nsuperior-quality homes that are priced well and marketed\nappropriately are selling quickly, according to White.\n\342\200\234In\302\240Connecticut, Leslie McElwreath, senior global real\nestate advisor, Sotheby\342\200\231s International Realty - Greenwich\nBrokerage, doubled the number of US$10 million-plus\ndeals in 2025 compared to 2019, even though there were\nfewer than 100 homes on the real estate market in that\nprice range,\342\200\235 White says.\n\342\200\234On Sea Island, Georgia, Chase Mizell of Atlanta Fine\nHomes Sotheby\342\200\231s International Realty and Susan Imhoff\nand Ann Harrell of DeLoach Sotheby\342\200\231s International Realty\nset a state record by selling architect John Portman\342\200\231s\n13,000-square-foot home for US$30 million,\342\200\2356 White\nadds. \342\200\234The house, Entelechy II, is strikingly contemporary,\na departure from the traditional cottages on the island,)/P 55 0 R/K[3601 0 R]/Pg 20 0 R/S/Figure>>
