2872 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(but it\342\200\231s right on the\302\240water.\342\200\235 That record could\nsoon be broken, however, by the former home of\nHGTV co-founder Ken Lowe and his wife Julia\342\200\224\na custom-built, 11,000-square-foot oceanfront\nestate\342\200\224according to an April 2026 report by The\nWall Street Journal.7 The mansion, called Lowe Tide,\nwas recently listed at US$42 million with\302\240DeLoach\nSotheby\342\200\231s International Realty.\nIn the wider real estate market, Hepp notes\na divergence between a slowing property market in\nthe Southeast compared to a more stable one in the\nMidwest and the Northeast. \342\200\234The general Florida housing\nmarket has slowed because of the compound effect of\nnatural disasters, higher insurance and immigration\nrestrictions, but high-end homebuyers\nseem to be insulated from those\302\240issues,\342\200\235 she\302\240says.\nThe ultra-luxury property market in Miami, Florida,\nis\302\240on particularly solid ground, according to Yun. \342\200\234They\nhad\302\240a\302\240little oversupply, but with their infrastructure\ndevelopment and new luxury condominium construction,\nit\342\200\231s becoming an even bigger city,\342\200\235 he says. \342\200\234There are\nmany, many million-dollar homes there, but the job\ngains\302\240in\302\240Florida have been growing faster than in the\nrest\302\240of\302\240the\302\240country.\342\200\235\nYun also believes many retiring wealthy baby\nboomers\302\240\(those born between 1946 and 1964\) will\nchoose\302\240to relocate to Florida in the years ahead,\nespecially\302\240to benefit from the lack of state income taxes\nthere. \342\200\234We\342\200\231ve seen renewed luxury real estate demand\nin\302\240New York City and California\342\200\231s Central Coast, but also\nbooming luxury property markets in Montana and\nWyoming, which are tax-friendly states,\342\200\235 Hepp says.\nIn Los Angeles, California, the \342\200\234mansion tax\342\200\235 on\nthe\302\240sale of properties worth US$5 million and more\nhas\302\240been in place\302\240since April 2023, yet the ultra-luxury\nproperty market there continues to thrive, Hepp says.\n\342\200\234Sales of homes priced from US$3 million to US$5 million\n[and so\302\240not subject to the additional tax] were up 11%\nin\302\2402025, while sales of homes at US$5 million and higher\nwere up\302\24030%.\342\200\235\nWhile Washington, D.C. was the focus of attention\nin\302\2402025 because of federal government layoffs, Yun says\nthe city\342\200\231s enduring appeal as an international capital has\nkept the ultra-luxury property market there thriving.\nHe\302\240says people with a long-term perspective are eager\nto\302\240get into the Washington, D.C. housing market now)/P 55 0 R/K[3606 0 R]/Pg 21 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

2873 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(because of the perception of a slowdown there,\nwhich\302\240has\302\240kept sales activity on solid\302\240ground.\nGlobally, sales transactions for the Sotheby\342\200\231s\nInternational Realty brand were up in 2025, White says.\nCabo\302\240San Lucas, Mexico, was among the stronger-\nperforming markets, part of what White describes\nas\302\240a\302\240genuine shift in homebuyer behavior. \342\200\234Americans\nare\302\240more open to different places than in the past,\342\200\235 he\nsays, a\302\240trend the brand is seeing across its global portfolio.\nVietnam represents the brand\342\200\231s next move in that\ndirection, a market where economic growth has created\na\302\240new class of wealthy domestic buyers, international\ninterest\302\240is accelerating and luxury inventory hasn\342\200\231t caught\nup\302\240with demand.\nThe country will join the\302\240brand\342\200\231s existing presence in key\nglobal hotspots in the\302\240Asia Pacific region, such as Australia,\nNew Zealand, Hong\302\240Kong, Singapore, Taiwan, the Philippines\nand Japan. \342\200\234Tokyo had an\302\240exceptional year, and Osaka opens\nup an entirely different side of what Japan has to offer our\nclients,\342\200\235 White says.\nLuxury homebuyers who rely on the brand\342\200\231s network\nare\302\240a mix of pure property investors and those looking for\na\302\240lifestyle purchase, according to White. \342\200\234Some homebuyers\nare just fascinated by real estate and want to buy multiple\nproperties with the potential to rent them for a season or\ntwo.\302\240But in the long term, they focus on getting a good price\nfor\302\240anything they buy. They need to see the value in their\npurchases and want to know that if and when they decide\nto\302\240sell, they have the potential to get a good return on\ntheir\302\240investment.\342\200\235\nThe Global Wealth Effect\nWealth continued to accumulate internationally in 2025,\nwith\302\240an estimated 41.3 million high-net-worth individuals\n\(HNWIs\) around the world, each with households worth\nmore\302\240than US$1 million, according to the World Ultra\nWealth\302\240Report 2025 released in September 2025 by\nAltrata,\302\240a provider of global financial data.8 Within that\ngroup\302\240there are more than 500,000 ultra-high-net-worth\nindividuals \(UHNWIs\), with more than US$30 million in\nwealth. And\302\240while\302\240UHNWIs make up\302\240just 1.1% of the\nworld\342\200\231s\302\240millionaires, an already rarefied demographic,\nthey\302\240hold 32% of this group\342\200\231s net worth, according to\nAltrata\342\200\231s\302\240research. u)/P 55 0 R/K[3607 0 R]/Pg 21 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

