2918 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(Boston and Cambridge,\nMassachusetts\nIn Boston, luxury condominium buildings\nin prime locations with high-end amenities\nattract plenty of homebuyers, but the\ntop range of the housing market in nearby\nCambridge primarily consists of single-\nfamily homes priced at US$10 million\nand\302\240above, according to Lauren Holleran,\nsenior global real estate advisor,\nGibson\302\240Sotheby\342\200\231s International Realty\nin\302\240Cambridge.)/P 55 0 R/K[3641 0 R]/Pg 25 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

2919 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(\342\200\234The luxury condominium market\nin\302\240Boston attracts people who want to\ndownsize from a larger house that needs\nwork,\342\200\235 Holleran says. \342\200\234In Cambridge, the\nupper end of the property market is mostly\nrenovated or remodeled single-family\nhomes that don't need any work done.\nWhat sells here is a Victorian exterior with\na beautifully renovated interior \342\200\223 done well,\nthat is a surefire winner in our market.\342\200\235\nThe appetite for renovating a home has\ndisappeared in the last year or two, Holleran\nexplains, primarily because of\nthe uncertainty of how much the work)/P 55 0 R/K[3642 0 R]/Pg 25 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

2920 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(will cost and how much time might be\nneeded to\302\240complete a major project.\n\342\200\234There was a price shift in our market,\nwith most ultra-luxury homes valued under\nUS$10 million rising to the US$15 million\nto US$16 million range by 2025,\342\200\235 she\nsays. \342\200\234I think we\342\200\231ve reached the top of the\nmarket of what homebuyers are willing to\npay now, so\302\240prices are pulling back to the\nUS$12\302\240million to US$15 million range.\342\200\235\nThe reason, she believes, is the\n\342\200\234vibecession\342\200\235\342\200\224the perception that\nthe\302\240economy is in a slowdown even\nwhen it\342\200\231s\302\240not.\302\240u)/P 55 0 R/K[3643 0 R]/Pg 25 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

