3146 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(as\302\240well\302\240as build a legacy. And\302\240increasingly, many older\nhomeowners prefer to upgrade or retrofit their current\nhomes to accommodate their needs as they age,\nas\302\240opposed to relocating.\n\342\200\234Among our international clientele, we clearly see\naffluent homebuyers retaining residential properties for\nmuch longer than originally planned,\342\200\235 says Despina Laou,\nhead of private office, Greece Sotheby\342\200\231s International\nRealty. \342\200\234Homes initially acquired as second residences\nare\302\240increasingly used as semi-permanent or permanent\nbases later in life. These individuals have the financial\nflexibility to live independently across multiple homes. What\nwe observe instead in Greece is a deliberate choice\302\240to age\nwell.\342\200\235)/P 55 0 R/K[3760 0 R]/Pg 36 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

3147 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(Laou cites as an example a couple from Australia,\nin\302\240their 70s, who acquired a property in Greece valued\nat\302\240approximately US$11.6 million. \342\200\234The home was\nchosen for long-term living, with multiple bedrooms\nto host children, grandchildren and permanent staff,\342\200\235\nshe explains. \342\200\234They now spend the Australian winter\n[June to August] in\302\240Greece\342\200\224effectively living a life\naligned with extended summer seasons.\342\200\235\nDesigning for Longer Living\nFor homebuyers planning to age in place, traditional luxury\nfeatures such as grand views or oversized entertaining\nspaces are now complemented by wellness-centric design.\n\342\200\234Affluent owners living longer will prioritize residences\nthat extend independent living\342\200\224with fall\342\200\221prevention\nlayouts, circadian lighting, air/water quality systems\nand integrated telehealth,\342\200\235 says Fahmi. \342\200\234Properties that\nembed age\342\200\221friendly design with sophisticated wellness\ntech will command a premium over comparable trophy\nassets without it. Homes with main\342\200\221floor suites, elevator\nstacks, slip\342\200\221resistant surfaces, smart monitoring, staff\nquarters and wellness suites will be at a premium.\342\200\235\nNearly 40% of real estate professionals cited in\nthe 2026 Mid-Year Sotheby\342\200\231s International Realty agent)/P 55 0 R/K[3761 0 R]/Pg 36 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

