3163 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(Loma Linda, California; and the Nicoya Peninsula,\nCosta\302\240Rica.5 These locations are consistently cited as\nexamples of exceptional longevity and quality of life.\nThese regions share a variety of characteristics\nincreasingly reflected in luxury real estate preferences:\nan\302\240emphasis on walkability, social connectedness,\naccess\302\240to nature, a nutritious local food system and\ncommunity-oriented design. Wealthy homebuyers\nare paying attention.\n\342\200\234More and more clients approach us with clear\nlongevity criteria\342\200\224outdoor activity, social connection,\nyear-round use and access to healthcare\342\200\224positioning\nGreece as a country where people choose to live longer\nand better,\342\200\235 Laou says. \342\200\234A notable example is a Swiss\ncouple in their early 60s who acquired a large estate in\nPorto Heli with the explicit intention of creating a long-\nterm base focused on wellness and longevity. Similar\nmotivations are increasingly seen in Paros and other\nquieter Cycladic islands.\342\200\235\nReal estate professionals in Costa Rica are\nnavigating similar desires. \342\200\234Within the Nicoya Peninsula,\ncommunities such as Nosara, Santa Teresa and Mal Pa\303\255s\nhave become natural magnets for longevity-minded\nhomebuyers,\342\200\235 says Elena Araya Call\303\255s, country manager,\nCosta Rica Sotheby\342\200\231s International Realty. \342\200\234What attracts\nthem is not spectacle but rhythm\342\200\224a way of life that feels\ngrounded, sustainable and deeply human.\342\200\235\nA compelling example of this approach is CalaSol,\na\302\240new residential enclave located directly within the Blue\nZone, she says. \342\200\234Set in Playa Gringo, Guanacaste, CalaSol\nreflects a new generation of luxury development\342\200\224one\nthat\302\240values permanence over pace and stewardship over\nscale,\342\200\235 Call\303\255s says. \342\200\234With just 32 dramatic ocean-view\nhomesites and direct adjacency to protected coastline,\nthe\302\240project prioritizes timelessness over volume and\nlegacy over yield. For its residents, CalaSol is not viewed)/P 55 0 R/K[3784 0 R]/Pg 38 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

3164 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(as a speculative property investment. It is\na multigenerational lifestyle decision. What is\nbeing acquired is not only land or architecture but\ncontinuity\342\200\224the assurance that the\302\240landscape, the\nview and the experience of place will\302\240endure.\342\200\235\nA site in Queenstown, New Zealand, has similar\nappeal\302\240to those seeking luxury and longevity, Fahmi\nsays. \342\200\234There\302\240is an exciting new development on the\nSouth Island, Te\302\240Taumata | Lakeview, represented by\nNew Zealand Sotheby\342\200\231s International Realty, where\nculture, health, wellness and creativity converge,\342\200\235 she\nexplains. \342\200\234Due to its location among local rivers and\nstreams, the development\342\200\231s central amenity hub Te Huika\nis where the community can come together. It also has\na world-class fitness center, spa, wellness center, boutique\nhotel, co-working space and a range of dining and retail\noptions. The art gallery is a standout feature, showcasing\nwork by acclaimed international and New Zealand artists\nand hosting exhibitions, workshops and cultural events.\nProjects like these focus on longevity.\342\200\235\nChanging Trends in Health\nand Home\nAs longevity continues to move from niche trend to\na defining economic and lifestyle force, luxury real\nestate stands at a compelling intersection of health\nand home. Ultimately, the aging millionaire boom is\nreshaping the real estate market: affluent homebuyers\nare not following old retirement playbooks but creating\nnew ones\342\200\224building and buying properties that support\nextended lifespans, deeper well-being and richer life\nexperiences. \342\200\234In this era of longevity, luxury real estate\nis no longer just about where you live but how well and\nhow long you can live there,\342\200\235 Fahmi says. \342\226\240)/P 55 0 R/K[3785 0 R]/Pg 38 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

3165 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(\nHomes are becoming hubs for care, connection\nand continuity\342\200\224where luxury is also defined\nby adaptability, wellness and community.\n\n\ntammy fahmi, senior vice president, global servicing and strategy, Sotheby\342\200\231s International Realty)/P 55 0 R/K[3786 0 R]/Pg 38 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

