<</Type/StructElem/Alt(Located on Via Monti, one\nof Milan\342\200\231s most exclusive\nresidential streets, an elegant\napartment offers a rare balance\nof refined neighborhood charm\nand city-center convenience.)/P 55 0 R/K[3841 0 R]/Pg 45 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

3245 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(Nuova were redeveloped into a bustling business district\nfocusing on finance, fashion and media. The city started\nto build international attention, first with the Expo 2015\nworld fair, and more recently as the host of the 2026\nWinter Games, according to a February 2026 report by\nAP News.12 Many Italian and international companies,\nfrom Prada and Versace to banking and energy firms,\nare now headquartered there, attracting sophisticated\nglobal buyers.\nItaly\342\200\231s flat tax, which caps foreign income tax for\nhomeowners at EU\342\202\254300,000 \(US$351,000\) annually,\nhas attracted a new set of property buyers to Milan,\naccording to Diletta Giorgolo, global real estate advisor,\nItaly Sotheby\342\200\231s International Realty. Others want to take\nadvantage of Italy\342\200\231s Residence by Investment Program,\nwhich starts at EU\342\202\254250,000 \(US$292,000\) according\nto the country\342\200\231s Ministry of Enterprises, and allows\nrecipients to travel freely through Europe.13\n\342\200\234That has attracted a lot of ultra-high-net-worth\nindividuals \(UHNWIs\),\342\200\235 says Giorgolo. \342\200\234More people\nwere coming to Italy for not only residency, but their\nfiscal regime. We were always used to international\nbuyers, but they came for second homes. The big\ndifference is that now many are buying primary homes.\342\200\235\nMilan took 11th place in a ranking of the cities with\nthe most millionaires, according to an April 2025 report\nby global wealth advisors Henley & Partners.14 People are\ncoming to the city from the U.K., the U.S., Canada and\neven France, where taxes are high, she explains.\nThe flat tax is particularly appealing for families\nliving in the U.K. who previously benefited from that\ncountry\342\200\231s non-domiciled tax regime, which exempted\naffluent foreign nationals from paying tax on their\noverseas investments. Since that program ended last\nyear, Milan\342\200\231s popularity has only increased, and it is now\none of the most requested urban destinations in the\ncountry for foreign homebuyers, according to Giorgolo.\nMilan\342\200\231s schools draw families to the city, while\nentrepreneurs are attracted by its business climate and\nlocation, she adds. Milan is \342\200\234in the center of Europe,\342\200\235\nGiorgolo notes. \342\200\234You can travel quickly to Austria, France,\nSwitzerland, Germany, so there are many advantages.\342\200\235\nVillas with gardens and penthouses are among\nthe most coveted property types, according to Giorgolo.\nMany homebuyers are looking for residences with historic\nfacades that have been gut-renovated to make way for\nultra-modern interiors, she says.\nResidential assets in Milan see consistent growth,\nwith \342\200\234appreciation around 3% to 4%. Some have had a 7%\nincrease, but it\342\200\231s a continuous, steady growth,\342\200\235 she says.\nStill, Milan offers relative affordability. \342\200\234In comparison to)/P 55 0 R/K[3842 0 R]/Pg 46 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

3246 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(other big capitals, Milan\342\200\224even if there are some very\nhigh square-meter prices right now\342\200\224is still affordable in\nrespect to other cities,\342\200\235 Giorgolo notes, adding that the\ngeneral cost of living in the city is also good. \342\200\234Universities\nare less expensive, and so are restaurants.\342\200\235\nInventory in Milan, like so many other luxury\nresidential destinations, is extremely limited. That\342\200\231s\nespecially true for move-in-ready homes, which are rare\nand sell very quickly, she adds. Plus, Italians are very\nhouse proud, with around 80% of residents owning their\nown home. Those residents do not move often, instead\nconsidering homes \342\200\234part of their family and heritage.\342\200\235\nBut when families are ready to sell, trophy assets\nin Milan\342\200\224and throughout Italy\342\200\224go very quickly, according\nto Giorgolo. Prices for the most sought-after estates can\nclimb as high as EU\342\202\25430 million \(US$35 million\).\nMilan continues to attract the elite buyers because of\nits economic engine, as well as the lifestyle it provides and\nthe favorable tax environment. \342\200\234It\342\200\231s still a very human-sized\ncapital,\342\200\235 Giorgolo says. \342\200\234It\342\200\231s also the closeness to so many\nother important places, the international schools, and that\nthe prices are continuing to grow at a very good pace.\342\200\235\nHong Kong, China\nAfter years of oversupply, Hong Kong is bouncing\nback, according to Teresa Chan, director of business\ndevelopment, List Sotheby\342\200\231s International Realty, Hong\nKong. \342\200\234Total transactions reached about 62,000 units\nfor\302\2402025, up 17% from 2024, with primary [home] sales\nmaking up 33%,\342\200\235 she explains, noting that overall house\nprices were up 1.13% year-over-year in October 2025.\n\342\200\234Supply remains high, with 27,000 unsold units\nand\302\24020,000 new completions expected in 2026.\342\200\235\nThe pandemic was hard on Hong Kong, with\nrestrictions and economic uncertainty slowing the city\342\200\231s\nproperty market until only recently. Home prices in the\ncity rose 3.3% in 2025, the first rise since 2021, Reuters\nreported, citing government data.15 \342\200\234On the sales side,\nactivity has continued to improve since March 2026.\n\342\200\234Transaction volumes are recovering gradually, led by\nthe primary market, supported by stabilizing interest\nrates and improved sentiment following Chinese New\nYear,\342\200\235 Chan says. \342\200\234Homebuyers remain selective and\nprice\342\200\221conscious, but liquidity has clearly improved\nwhen pricing is realistic.\342\200\235\nIn addition, global uncertainty has reinforced Hong\nKong\342\200\231s position as a relatively safe haven for some\nUHNWIs, Chan notes. \342\200\234We are seeing growing interest\nfrom regional homebuyers and families reassessing)/P 55 0 R/K[3843 0 R]/Pg 46 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

