3250 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(geographic exposure, with Hong Kong viewed as a stable\nbase for both capital preservation and long\342\200\221term living.\342\200\235\nMainland Chinese residents make up as much\nas 30%\302\240of homebuyers in Hong Kong, she adds, with\nUHNWIs from tech sectors and returning overseas\nproperty investors also showing interest. Brand-new\nluxury apartments and condominiums in areas such as\nThe Peak and Mid-Levels are the hottest type of\302\240residence,\nwith older buildings only selling at a premium if they\342\200\231ve\nbeen renovated, Chan explains.\nIn the longer term, real estate investors can expect\na healthy profit, according to Chan. \342\200\234Prices are forecast\nto rise 3% to 5% in 2026,\342\200\235 she says, adding that luxury\nresidences could see up to 5% appreciation. \342\200\234ROI depends\non the holding period. The long-term is positive due to\nrecovery, but the short-term can be volatile.\342\200\235\nOne plus: Hong Kong abolished all additional taxes\nfor residential property buyers in early 2024, including the\nBuyer\342\200\231s Stamp Duty and the Special Stamp Duty, she adds.\nAll buyers, whether permanent residents or not,\nare now subject to the same standard stamp duty,\nwhich has progressive rates based on property value.\nThe maximum rate is 4.25% for properties valued at or\nabove HK$21.74 million \(US$2.8 million\), Chan says.\nShe also notes that Hong Kong offers investment-\nlinked residency for those who make a HK$30 million\n\(US$3.85 million\) investment in the city, including\nproperty, via the New Capital Investment Entrant\nScheme.16 This program was relaunched in March 2024\nto help attract buyers, with the city expanding eligible)/P 55 0 R/K[3847 0 R]/Pg 47 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

3251 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/Alt(investments and pushing to establish family offices\nwith tax concessions. \342\200\234It\342\200\231s all designed to boost the\ncity\342\200\231s luxury property market and overall financial hub\nstatus,\342\200\235 Chan says.\nInstitutional stability, a strategic economic location\nand a high quality of life are the big draws for buyers,\nshe adds. \342\200\234The city\342\200\231s adherence to an independent\ncommon law legal system provides a reliable foundation\nfor investment, while its simple and competitive tax\nregime enhances wealth preservation.\342\200\235\nWith its location near mainland China and the\nother municipalities of the Greater Bay Area\342\200\224which\nincludes Macau, Guangzhou and Shenzhen\342\200\224Hong\nKong \342\200\234offers unparalleled access to regional economic\ngrowth,\342\200\235 Chan adds. \342\200\234This is complemented by world-\nclass infrastructure, a dense network of amenities\nand a vibrant international culture that collectively\nmake it uniquely appealing for both property investment\nand living.\342\200\235\nUrban Appeal\nCities are the global engines of the economy\342\200\224and there\nare always homebuyers lining up who want a piece of\nthe action. Urban areas maintain their appeal by offering\naccess to the arts, culture and people, sophisticated\nhousing options and strong infrastructure. For many,\nit\342\200\231s the combination of energy and opportunity that\nkeeps them within city limits. \342\226\240)/P 55 0 R/K[3848 0 R]/Pg 47 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

